        rdfs:comment        "Xbp-1 (S) binds the sequence CCACG in ER Stress Responsive Elements (ERSE, consensus sequence CCAAT (N)9 CCACG) located upstream from many genes. The ubiquitous transcription factor NF-Y, a heterotrimer, binds the CCAAT portion of the ERSE and together the IRE1-alpha: NF-Y complex activates transcription of a set of chaperone genes including DNAJB9, EDEM, RAMP4, p58IPK, and others. This results in an increase in protein folding activity in the ER." ;
        rdfs:label          "XBP1(S) activates chaperone genes" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: May, B, 2009-06-02 00:51:49" , "Reviewed: Urano, F, 2010-04-30" , "Reviewed: D'Eustachio, P, Matthews, L, Gillespie, ME, 2008-12-02 16:25:31" , "Edited: May, B, 2009-06-02 00:51:49" , "GOC:reactome_curators" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-381038" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-381070/R-HSA-381070> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

